From ad3b1eba4b714cd0e80c39d44d33239a52e225d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:16:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Forward explicit bounded allocator opt-in through
 test runner

Problem: whole-file offline tests exhausted a 3 GiB address-space limit while RSS stayed below the cgroup limit; component and clean-base controls both failed.
Why: retained maps showed large glibc arena reservations. An explicit MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2 paired control passed 19/19 on each tree with sharply reduced reserved address space.
Why the control was unavailable: the canonical runner's env -i discarded the allocator setting. Existing tests did not exercise this opt-in across actual activation/reexec and final pytest children.

Forward only an explicitly supplied canonical decimal 1..1024. Keep absent behavior unchanged and reject invalid values before Python/setup/test children. No general environment passthrough, global default, cap changes or runtime changes.

Proof: real-shell RED 1 passed/3 failed before forwarding; GREEN 35 passed/0 failed with explicit/current/missing/stale activation and stale-refresh refusal. Full scripts/check: 21 checks OK. Source hashes and raw logs independently rechecked before publication. Prior whole-file failures remain retained, not erased by conditional controls.

Coverage limits: Linux resource receipts only; offline fixture provisioning is not locked-install proof. Failed-refresh case is successful setup leaving stale stamps, not nonzero setup exit. Invalid input executes explicit/missing paths; other paths share the early guard. Final child isolation covers three synthetic sentinels, not comprehensive intermediate-process isolation. Prepublication independent source assessment is not exact-head ship approval.

Separate harness-only delivery; no machine-component, parser or fleet remediation bundled. Original no-model-pin goal and remaining consumer ledger stay open.
